euthydemus-learn.logic.r1: argue/two-senses: C (S17): "learning" is taken as grasping or understanding what is said, as with the dictation in C and as acquiring from teachers knowledge one does not yet have where learner is used else, a reader says
euthydemus-learn.logic.r1: argue/two-senses: C (S17): "unlearned" is taken as dull or slow, the opposite of the clever wise boys in C and as not knowing what one is learning where unlearned_k is used else, a reader says
